		<title><![CDATA[Episode 5: Small Talk, Diesel: Running on Gas, Ask OTC, Unchained Melodies, and Shantideva]]></title>
		<link>https://otc.steelwagstaff.info/episode-5-small-talk-diesel-running-gas-ask-otc-unchained-melodies-shantideva/</link>
		<pubDate>Fri, 27 Feb 2015 13:00:26 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[steel]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://otc.awesomecity.org/?p=83</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[This week Dave and Steel are joined by their old friend Jordan, a Las Vegas-based lawyer. Together, the trio talk about professional dumpster divers, meditating mummified monks, and the maker Jimmy DiResta, introduce a new segment focused on Dave &amp; Jordan's shared love of Vin Diesel, take a question from a listener about how to deal with boring lecture classes, share some of their favorite recent music, and explore the wisdom of the 8th Century Buddhist monk Shantideva.
<h2>Links</h2>
<h3>Small Talk</h3>
<ul>
	<li>Wired Magazine's <a title="Wired profile of Matt Malone" href="http://www.wired.com/2015/02/high-end-dumpster-diving-matt-malone/" target="_blank">profile of Matt Malone</a>, professional dumpster diver in Austin, Texas.</li>
	<li>Story on <a title="BBC story on mummified Buddhist monk" href="http://www.bbc.com/news/world-asia-31125338" target="_blank">the unidentified mummified Buddhist monk</a> in Mongolia from the BBC. A more in-depth <a href="http://siberiantimes.com/other/others/news/n0105-mummified-monk-is-not-dead-and-in-rare-meditative-state-says-expert/" target="_blank">feature</a> appeared in the Siberian Times.</li>
	<li>Jimmy DiResta's <a title="Jimmy DiResta's YouTube channel" href="https://www.youtube.com/user/jimmydiresta" target="_blank">YouTube channel</a>. Jordan recommends starting with these two classics:
Making an Aluminum Hatchet Handle:
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=DFpIIM3b3TY
Making an AK47-shaped guitar for Wyclef Jean:
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eLmKrXjTwIo</li>
</ul>
<h3>Diesel: Running on Gas</h3>
Dave &amp; Jordan discuss the 2013 film <em>Riddick</em>, the third in the <a title="Chronicles of Riddick franchise" href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Chronicles_of_Riddick_%28franchise%29" target="_blank">Chronicles of Riddick franchise</a>. Here's the film's trailer [warning: it's pretty intense and probably not for children]:
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=au2xw42-8IA
<h3>Ask OTC</h3>
Here are a couple of images Dave and Jordan have drawn in class to help them pass the time.

[caption id="attachment_99" align="alignnone" width="850"]<img class="size-full wp-image-99" src="http://otc.steelwagstaff.info/wp-content/uploads/sites/8/2015/02/geometric-patterns.jpg" alt="Geometric Patterns" width="850" height="670" /> Geometric Pattern sketch made by Jordan during a law school course.[/caption]

[caption id="attachment_101" align="alignnone" width="850"]<img class="size-full wp-image-101" src="http://otc.steelwagstaff.info/wp-content/uploads/sites/8/2015/02/gentlemail.jpg" alt="Gentle Bear checks his mail. " width="850" height="705" /> In this drawing by Dave, Gentle Bear checks his mail.[/caption]
Dave has published a whole book of Gentle Bear cartoons, called <em>Gentle Bear: Gentle Honey</em> which you can buy in <a href="http://www.amazon.com/Gentle-Bear-Honey-Dave-Jenson-ebook/dp/B009NUKBJI/" title="Gentle Bear: Gentle Honey" target="_blank">eBook form</a>.
<h3>Unchained Melodies</h3>
DakhaBrakha: Baby
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r0AYokGJD6I
Animals as Leaders: Lippincott
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8saKHKt1A5Q
AC/DC: Thunderstruck
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=v2AC41dglnM
Liam Bailey: Stun Me
<span><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7oqyJYV60yE" title="Stun Me by Liam Bailey on Grooveshark">Stun Me by Liam Bailey on Grooveshark</a></span>
Alash Ensemble: Bashtak

<h3>Book Wisdom</h3>
This week's Book Wisdom was stitched together from various passages in Vesna A. and B. Alan Wallace's translation of Shantideva's <a title="Santideva's A Guide to the Bodhisattva Way of Life" href="http://www.shambhala.com/a-guide-to-the-bodhisattva-way-of-life.html" target="_blank"><em>A Guide to the Bodhisattva Way of Life</em></a>.]]></content:encoded>
		<excerpt:encoded><![CDATA[]]></excerpt:encoded>
