		<title><![CDATA[Episode 8: Children&#039;s Picture Books, Small Talk, Ask OTC, Unchained Melodies, and The English Patient]]></title>
		<link>https://otc.steelwagstaff.info/episode-8-childrens-picture-books-small-talk-ask-otc-unchained-melodies-and-the-english-patient/</link>
		<pubDate>Fri, 20 Mar 2015 12:00:32 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[steel]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://otc.awesomecity.org/?p=152</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[This week Dave and Steel are joined by their old friend <a href="http://clubnarwhal.blogspot.com/p/about.html" target="_blank">Amy</a> to discuss children's picture books, cave dwellings, pigeon-based Ponzi schemes, a once in a lifetime chance to own Hell, frog burgers, answer pressing questions from longtime listeners, share some of their favorite recent music, and drop some beauty from Michael Ondaatje.

<h2>Links</h2>
<h3>Children's Picture Books</h3>
<h4>Dave's recommendations</h4>
<ul>
	<li><a href="http://www.peggyrathmann.com/" title="Peggy Rathmann" target="_blank">Peggy Rathmann</a>: She's my number one. We especially love <em><a href="http://www.peggyrathmann.com/goodnightgorilla.html" target="_blank">Good Night, Gorilla</a></em></li>
<li><a href="http://www.mowillems.com/" title="Mo Willems" target="_blank">Mo Willems</a>. Especially the <a href="http://www.pigeonpresents.com/books.aspx" title="Elephant &amp; Piggie books" target="_blank">Elephant &amp; Piggie series</a>.</li>
	<li><a href="http://us.macmillan.com/author/urishulevitz" title="Uri Shulevitz" target="_blank">Uri Shulevitz</a>. Especially his book <em><a href="http://us.macmillan.com/snow/urishulevitz" title="Uri Shulevitz' Snow" target="_blank">Snow</a></em></li></ul>
<h4>Amy's recommendations</h4>
<ul>
	<li>Harry G. Allard's <em><a href="http://www.amazon.com/Miss-Nelson-Missing-Harry-Allard/dp/0395401461" title="Miss Nelson is Missing!" target="_blank">Miss Nelson is Missing!</a>, illustrated by James Marshall.</em></li>
	<li><a href="http://www.veryawesomeworld.com/" target="_blank">Dallas Clayton</a>'s <em><a href="http://www.amazon.com/dp/0062114689/ref=as_li_ss_til?tag=thepaperbriga-20&amp;camp=0&amp;creative=0&amp;linkCode=as4&amp;creativeASIN=0062114689&amp;adid=1JBTWSNRRAJWETMFT5DM" title="Dallas Clayton's An Awesome Book" target="_blank">An Awesome Book</a></em>.</li>
	<li>B.J. Novak's <em><a href="http://www.amazon.com/The-Book-Pictures-B-J-Novak/dp/0803741715" title="B.J. Novak's The Book with No Pictures" target="_blank">The Book with No Pictures</a></em>.
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cREyQJO9EPs
</li></ul>
<h4>Steel's recommendations</h4>
<ul>
	<li>Richard Scarry. Especially <em><a href="http://www.amazon.com/What-Do-People-All-Day/dp/0394818237" title="What Do People Do All Day?" target="_blank">What do People Do All Day?</a></em> and <em><a href="http://www.amazon.com/Richard-Scarrys-Cars-Trucks-Things/dp/0307157857/ref=asap_bc?ie=UTF8" title="Cars and Trucks and Things That Go" target="_blank">Cars and Trucks and Things That Go</a></em>.</li>
	<li>Oscar Wilde's <em><a href="http://www.amazon.com/Selfish-Giant-Michael-Neugebauer-book/dp/1558582932/kevinholtsber-20" title="The Selfish Giant" target="_blank">The Selfish Giant</a></em>, with watercolor illustrations by Lizbeth Zwerger.</li>
	<li>Ingri and Edgar d'Aulaire's <em><a href="http://www.amazon.com/DAulaires-Norse-Myths-Ingri-dAulaire/dp/159017125X" title="Book of Norse Myths" target="_blank">Book of Norse Myths</a></em> and <em><a href="http://www.amazon.com/DAulaires-Greek-Myths-Ingri-dAulaire/dp/0440406943" title="Book of Greek Myths" target="_blank">Book of Greek Myths</a></em>.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Small Talk</h3>
<a href="http://io9.com/remarkable-cave-houses-including-the-homes-that-inspir-502255017" title="Remarkable Cave Homes" target="_blank">Dave's favorite cave homes.</a>
<a href="http://www.freep.com/story/news/local/michigan/2015/02/13/michigan-sale-tourist-trap/23365367/" target="_blank">Hell [Michican] for sale</a> and the <a href="http://www.freep.com/story/news/local/michigan/2015/02/26/michigan-kickstarter-campaign/24054799/" target="_blank">Damned artists who want to buy it</a>. Amy's list of her <a href="http://clubnarwhal.blogspot.com/2013/10/Things-To-Do-in-Hell-Michigan.html" target="_blank">top 5 things to do in Hell</a>.
Jon Mooallem's story about <a href="http://www.nytimes.com/2015/03/05/magazine/the-pigeon-king-and-the-ponzi-scheme-that-shook-canada.html" target="_blank">Arlan Galbraith, the Ponzi-scheming Pigeon King</a>.
And, ummm, don't forget about <a href="http://www.dailymail.co.uk/travel/travel_news/article-2986230/Frog-throat-Japanese-nature-museum-launches-FROG-burgers-celebrate-new-poisonous-creatures-section.html" target="_blank">frog burgers</a>.
<h3>Ask OTC</h3>
The <a href="http://www.stuffedanimals.com/stuffed_animal_hospital_a/164.htm" title="Stuffed Animal Hospital" target="_blank">stuffed animal hospital</a> that just might be what you need to revive your best friend from childhood.
Amy's got a whole bunch of <a href="http://clubnarwhal.blogspot.com/p/food.html" target="_blank">recipes</a> on her blog, including this mouthwatering one for <a href="http://clubnarwhal.blogspot.com/2015/01/skinny-texas-cheese-fries.html" target="_blank">Skinny Texas Cheese Fries</a>.
<a href="http://techcrunch.com/2013/09/09/watch-the-real-life-taco-copter-drop-some-delicious-mexican-food-from-20-feet/" target="_blank">The tacocopter</a>. Apparently they're <a href="http://tacocopter.com/" target="_blank">trying it out in San Francisco</a> (beta version), which of course they are.
<h3>Unchained Melodies</h3>
<h4>Caroline Smith -- Bloodstyle</h4>
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=P5ozDA-kKWk
<h4>Dom La Nena -- Llegaré</h4>
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ao2H-C9CIkA
<h4>Built to Spill -- Living Zoo</h4>
https://soundcloud.com/builttospill/living-zoo
<h4>The Decemberists -- Carolina Low</h4>
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EWpweCPUc-E
<h4>D'Angelo and the Vanguard -- Back to the Future (Part 1)</h4>
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ISCFeQ7963A
<h4>The Beatles -- Golden Slumbers</h4>
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ykl4Uqrbhjc
<h3>Book Wisdom</h3>
This week's passage comes from Michael Ondaatje's beautiful novel <em><a href="http://www.amazon.com/The-English-Patient-Michael-Ondaatje/dp/0679745203" target="_blank">The English Patient</a></em>.]]></content:encoded>
