		<title><![CDATA[Episode 16:  Disney World, Small Talk, Ask OTC, Expert Testimony: OTC Comics, Unchained Melodies, and The Phantom Tollbooth]]></title>
		<link>https://otc.steelwagstaff.info/episode-16-disney-world-small-talk-ask-otc-expert-testimony-otc-comics-unchained-melodies-and-the-phantom-tollbooth/</link>
		<pubDate>Fri, 15 May 2015 12:00:13 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[steel]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://otc.awesomecity.org/?p=223</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[This week Dave and Steel are joined by their friend Oliver. Together they discuss Dave's recent family vacation to Disney World (including a refreshing stop at Club Cool!), explore the benefits of Transcendental Meditation, learn more about the Rocky Mountain Land Library, speculate about the return of Full House (it's going to be called Fuller House!), offer listeners moving advice and dance tips, discuss Dave and Oliver's shared passion for cartooning and comic books, share their envy of the voices of Antony Heggarty, Prince Nelson, Van Morrison, Vic Chesnutt, Charlie Puth, and Bobby Hatfield &amp; Bill Medley, and drop some wisdom from Norton Juster's classic children's adventure novel The Phantom Tollbooth.
<h2>Links</h2>
<h3>Disney World</h3>
<a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mickey_Mouse_universe#Supporting_characters" target="_blank">Duffy the Disney Bear</a>
<a href="http://allears.net/tp/ep/ice.htm" target="_blank">Club Cool</a>
<h3>Small Talk</h3>
<h4>Transcendental Meditation</h4>
<ul>
	<li><a href="http://www.wnyc.org/story/jerry-seinfeld/#" target="_blank">Alec Baldwin and Jerry Seinfeld discuss Transcendental Meditation</a> on Here's the Thing.</li>
	<li><a href="https://www.mum.edu/about-mum/" target="_blank">The Maharishi University of Management</a> (which Steel kept mistakenly calling the Maharishi <em>Institute</em> of Management.</li>
	<li><a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Domes" target="_blank">The Golden Domes</a></li>
</ul>
<h4>The Rocky Mountain Land Library</h4>
<ul>
	<li><a href="http://www.nytimes.com/2015/04/17/us/envisioning-a-colorado-haven-for-readers-nestled-amid-mountains-of-books.html?_r=0" target="_blank">NYT article about the project</a></li>
	<li><a href="https://landlibrary.wordpress.com/" target="_blank">Official Website</a></li>
</ul>
<h4>TV Show Reunions</h4>
<ul>
	<li><a href="http://bgr.com/2015/04/07/arrested-development-season-5-release/" target="_blank">Arrested Development Season 5</a></li>
	<li><a href="http://showtimeallaccess.tumblr.com/post/99324820892/showtime-is-serving-up-some-damngoodcoffee-in" target="_blank">Twin Peaks coming back in 2016</a></li>
	<li><a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wet_Hot_American_Summer:_First_Day_of_Camp" target="_blank">Wet Hot American Summer</a></li>
	<li><a href="http://www.slashfilm.com/netflix-fuller-house/" target="_blank">Fuller House</a></li>
</ul>
<h3>Expert Testimony: OTC Comics</h3>
<ul>
<li>The <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bone_%28comics%29" target="_blank">Bone</a> Series</li>
<li><a href="http://familycircus.com/" target="_blank">Family Circus</a></li>
<li><a href="http://thenearsightedmonkey.tumblr.com/" target="_blank">Lynda Barry's Tumblr</a></li>
<li>John Porcellino's <em><a href="https://www.drawnandquarterly.com/hospital-suite" target="_blank">The Hospital Suite</a></em></li>
<li>Some of <a href="http://oliverbendorf.tumblr.com/comics" target="_blank">Oliver's art and illustration</a></li>
</ul>
<h3>Unchained Melodies</h3>
<h4>Antony and the Johnsons -- Dust &amp; Water</h4>
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Is3skKNNa1U
<h4>Prince -- <a href="http://www.myvideo.de/watch/6367094/Prince_Kiss" target="_blank">Kiss</a></h4>
<h4>Van Morrison -- Ballerina</h4>
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZdB5N4meH9g
<h4>Vic Chesnutt -- Flirted with You All My Life</h4>
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V4Z-kjr4BLs
<h4>Wiz Khalifa ft. Charlie Puth -- See You Again</h4>
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RgKAFK5djSk
<h4>Righteous Brothers -- Unchained Melody</h4>
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IYj2hex99gY
<h3>Book Wisdom</h3>
For this week's book wisdom, Oliver shared a lovely passage from Norton Juster's <em><a href="http://www.amazon.com/The-Phantom-Tollbooth-Norton-Juster/dp/0394820371" target="_blank">The Phantom Tollbooth</a></em> about how the watchdog Tock got his name.]]></content:encoded>
