		<title><![CDATA[Episode 35: We&#039;ve Got You Covered!]]></title>
		<link>https://otc.steelwagstaff.info/episode-35-weve-got-covered/</link>
		<pubDate>Fri, 09 Oct 2015 11:00:14 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[steel]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://otc.awesomecity.org/?p=365</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[This week Dave and Steel bring Zac back on the show to discuss the joys and terrors of fairs (County and State alike), the golden era of Pauly Shore films, a guy who surfed a 20 foot wave on a motorcycle with skis attached, and the new Alexander Hamilton hip-hop Broadway musical. They also have their first poetry face-off (Mary Oppen vs. David Berman), cover some zany corporate hijinks, play great cover songs by Earth, Wind, &amp; Fire, Pavement, M. Ward, Jamie Cullum, the Lemonheads, and Bonnie "Prince" Billy, and Steel shares some book wisdom from the poet Brian Teare.
<h2>Links</h2>
<h3>Small Talk</h3>
<ul>
	<li>Top 5 Pauly Shore films [Dave]</li>
	<li>Robbie Maddison surfed a 20 foot wave on a motorcycle with skis:
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lDi9uFcD7XI</li>
	<li>Alexander Hamilton, <a href="http://www.vox.com/2015/9/30/9419835/hamilton-musical-lin-manuel-miranda" target="_blank">the hip-hop musical</a></li>
</ul>
<h3>Unchained Melodies: Cover Me!</h3>
https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLcPWWK79NBW0VyUX-MUmQRzjs6Suy67In
<h3>Book Wisdom</h3>
This week's book wisdom was provided by <a href="http://www.brianteare.net/" target="_blank">Brian Teare</a>'s poem "<a href="https://www.poets.org/poetsorg/poem/when-we-are-right-track-we-are-rewarded-joy" target="_blank">When we are on the right track, we are surprised by joy</a>"

<small>Featured image by <a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/28618109@N05/3988357319" target="_blank">Robert Bejil Productions</a> <a title="Attribution License" href="http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><img src="http://otc.awesomecity.org/wp-content/plugins/wp-inject/images/cc.png" alt="" /></a></small>]]></content:encoded>
