		<title><![CDATA[Episode 38: All Hallows&#039; Eve!]]></title>
		<link>https://otc.steelwagstaff.info/episode-38-all-hallows-eve/</link>
		<pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2015 12:00:53 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[steel]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://otc.awesomecity.org/?p=390</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p class="p1">This week Dave and Steel are joined by Jordan for a special Halloween edition of the podcast. We discuss our all-time greatest Halloween costumes, share spooky stories, talk about scary films we've enjoyed, give an update on Vin Diesel and his latest Witch Hunter film, share spine-chilling tunes from Thurl Ravenscroft, Perfume Genius, Henry Hall, Nina Simone, Vince Staples, and Mastodon, and read a scary story to tell in the dark.</p>

<h2 class="p1">Links</h2>
<h3>Diesel: Running on Gas</h3>
<ul>
	<li><span style="font-weight: 400">Grantland's Shea Serrano developed a <a href="http://grantland.com/hollywood-prospectus/the-vin-diesel-character-matrix/" target="_blank">Vin Diesel character matrix</a> that we all agree is pretty accurate.</span></li>
	<li><span style="font-weight: 400">The folks at the Nerdist invited Vin to join a round of Dungeons and Dragons. They made a short teaser, called D&amp;Diesel:
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=SlWt07l_pvI
</span></li>
</ul>
<h3>Unchained Melodies: Spooky Songs Edition</h3>
https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLcPWWK79NBW3bgI4Rx9pailYPX5Cn_YHP
<h3>Book Wisdom</h3>
Jordan read "The White Wolf" from <em>Scary Stories to Tell in the Dark</em>, a book which features haunting tales collected and retold by Alvin Schwartz and very memorable illustrations by Stephen Gammell.

<small>Featured image by <a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/25814320@N02/10601198054" target="_blank">vandalog</a> <a title="Attribution-ShareAlike License" href="http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow"><img src="http://otc.awesomecity.org/wp-content/plugins/wp-inject/images/cc.png" alt="" /></a></small>]]></content:encoded>
