		<title><![CDATA[Episode 43: Our Favorite Things]]></title>
		<link>https://otc.steelwagstaff.info/episode-43-our-favorite-things/</link>
		<pubDate>Fri, 11 Dec 2015 13:00:06 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[steel]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://otc.awesomecity.org/?p=417</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[This week Dave and Steel take a page from the <a href="http://www.oprah.com/gift/Oprahs-Favorite-Things-2015" target="_blank">Oprah playbook</a> and discuss some of their favorite things from 2015. They also tell some stories about their kids, share great music from their favorite musicians: Pavement, Damien Jurado, Wilco, and M. Ward, and Steel reads George Oppen's poem "Psalm."

We're going to be taking next week off, so enjoy this one for the next little while. Here's our plan for the rest of the year: on Christmas Eve we'll release a very special present: Dave's 2015 family spoken word Christmas album, and we'll have a New Year's Eve episode with the year in review (our Best of 2015 episode). Hope you all have a safe, loving December.
<h2>Links</h2>
<h3>Our Favorite Things</h3>
<h4>Beverage</h4>
<ul>
<ul>
	<li>Dave - <a href="http://www.docholidaysoda.com/" target="_blank">Doc Holiday soda</a> or <a href="http://disneyparks.disney.go.com/blog/2012/09/a-sip-of-lefous-brew-from-gastons-tavern-in-new-fantasyland-at-magic-kingdom-park/" target="_blank">Le Fou’s brew</a></li>
	<li>Steel - cold water</li>
</ul>
</ul>
<h4>Live Performance Experience</h4>
<ul>
	<li>Steel - <a href="http://damienjurado.com/" target="_blank">Damien Jurado</a></li>
	<li>Dave - <a href="http://gregoryalanisakov.com/tour" target="_blank">Gregory Alan Isakov</a></li>
</ul>
<h4>Penis Shaped Bread Tridents</h4>
<ul>
	<li>Dave - <a href="http://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B016E6Y1G2/ref=s9_simh_gw_p325_d3_i1?pf_rd_m=ATVPDKIKX0DER&amp;pf_rd_s=desktop-1&amp;pf_rd_r=1Q417ERA3GX8Z4H7P1WY&amp;pf_rd_t=36701&amp;pf_rd_p=2079475242&amp;pf_rd_i=desktop#customerReviews" target="_blank">The one Oprah recommends</a>. The <a href="http://www.amazon.com/review/R3BIHQ28ZRDX6X/ref=cm_cr_dp_title?ie=UTF8&amp;ASIN=B016E6Y1G2&amp;channel=detail-glance&amp;nodeID=16310101&amp;store=grocery" target="_blank">best review</a> I saw was by Adam W:
<blockquote>For years, I've searched the internet for assorted-size bread penises. When I have found them, they're either way too expensive or uncircumcised. Well, now I don't have to worry about that. This is one amazing bread penis set. The best part is the single penis with two heads that tangles itself to form the base of this treat. I can't wait to gobble down every inch of this.</blockquote>
</li>
	<li>Steel - I'm partial to the bread penises baked by <a href="https://www.instagram.com/Weedpriest/" target="_blank">WeedPriest</a>, a <a href="http://www.buzzfeed.com/ryanhatesthis/subway-employees-fired-for-baking-bread-into-the-shape-of-pe#.bv7dzDvG2" target="_blank">former Subway employee</a> [Steel]</li>
</ul>
<h4>Salt</h4>
<ul>
	<li>Dave - <a href="http://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B016E7VGDW?redirect=true&amp;ref=oft15_B016E7VGDW_AL_74" target="_blank">The salt Oprah recommends</a>: <a href="http://www.amazon.com/review/R1XOVURH12CHSU/ref=cm_cr_dp_title?ie=UTF8&amp;ASIN=B016E7VGDW&amp;channel=detail-glance&amp;nodeID=16310101&amp;store=grocery">Great Salts And Functional 3-Tier Salt Storage Unit
</a></li>
	<li>Steel - <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salt_March" target="_blank">Gandhi’s salt</a></li>
</ul>
<h4>Mail order Catalog</h4>
<ul>
	<li>Dave - <a href="http://www.hammacher.com/CatalogRequest/Default.aspx?promo=left_cs_cat_req" target="_blank">Hammacher Schlemmer</a></li>
	<li>Steel - <a href="http://www.wsj.com/articles/j-c-penney-resurrects-its-catalog-1421695574" target="_blank">JC Penney</a> or <a href="http://www.spiegel.com/info/Catalog" target="_blank">Spiegel</a> [as a pre-teen. For the lingerie section]</li>
</ul>
<h4>Animal</h4>
<ul>
	<li>Dave - Giraffe</li>
	<li>Steel - Otter or capybara
[embed]https://www.facebook.com/photo.php?fbid=10208508797377064&amp;l=64aba3b14e[/embed]
<h4>Month</h4>
<ul>
	<li>Dave - May</li>
	<li>Steel - December</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<h4>Matching Family Pajama Set</h4>
<ul>
	<li>Dave - <a href="http://www.amazon.com/b/?&amp;node=13164741011&amp;ref=oft15_NA-020_AL_22" target="_blank">The one Oprah recommends</a></li>
	<li>Steel - TMNT. For <a href="http://www.target.com/p/men-s-tmnt-union-suit-with-cape-green/-/A-21562305?ci_src=17588969&amp;ci_sku=21562305&amp;ref=tgt_adv_XS000000&amp;AFID=google_pla_df&amp;CPNG=PLA_Men%2BShopping&amp;adgroup=Union+Suits_SC&amp;LID=700000001170770pgs&amp;network=g&amp;device=c&amp;location=9018944&amp;gclid=CO7AuMuxhMkCFYRCaQodsy8HrQ&amp;gclsrc=aw.ds">MEN</a> + <a href="http://www.target.com/p/tmnt-women-s-pj-sleep-unionsuit/-/A-21408856?ci_src=17588969&amp;ci_sku=21408856&amp;ref=tgt_adv_XS000000&amp;AFID=google_pla_df&amp;CPNG=PLA_Women%2BShopping&amp;adgroup=Union+Suits_SC&amp;LID=700000001170770pgs&amp;network=g&amp;device=c&amp;location=9018944&amp;gclid=CPj80syxhMkCFQkyaQodtjcDqg&amp;gclsrc=aw.ds">WOMEN</a></li>
</ul>
&nbsp;
<h4>Hat for a dog</h4>
<ul>
	<li>Dave - <a href="http://www.amazon.com/gp/product/B016QVYW3M?ref=oft15_B016QVYW3M_AL_30" target="_blank">The one Oprah recommends:</a> American Beagle Outfitters - <a href="http://www.amazon.com/dp/B016J6FWV0" target="_blank">Antler Beanie</a>.</li>
	<li>Steel - The one that the Grinch puts on Max to make him into a reindeer.
<img class="alignnone" src="https://i.ytimg.com/vi/L06ncrRF-jM/hqdefault.jpg" alt="Max with reindeer hat." width="480" height="360" /></li>
</ul>
&nbsp;
<h4>Dance Party Song</h4>
<ul>
	<li>Dave - Lotus Flower - Radiohead
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=cfOa1a8hYP8</li>
	<li>Steel - <a href="http://video.naij.com/view=vgc5mdw4" target="_blank">Kiss</a> - Prince</li>
</ul>
<h4>Place to take the kids on walks/outings</h4>
<ul>
	<li>Steel - The <a href="http://lakeshorepreserve.wisc.edu/visit/lakeshorepath.htm">lakeshore nature trail</a></li>
	<li>Dave - The high school track in Snowflake</li>
</ul>
<h4>Poem</h4>
<ul>
	<li>Dave - that one about <a href="http://www.poetryfoundation.org/poem/243834">the guy in WWII </a>talking to the shop keeper [it's by Charles Reznikoff -- ed. note]</li>
	<li>Steel - <a href="http://www.poetryfoundation.org/learning/guide/177375">Psalm</a> - George Oppen</li>
</ul>
<h4>Local Attraction</h4>
<ul>
	<li>Steel - <a href="http://mustardmuseum.com/" target="_blank">National Mustard Museum</a></li>
	<li>Dave - <a href="http://www.azgfd.gov/h_f/hatcheries_silver_creek.shtml" target="_blank">Silver Creek fish hatchery</a></li>
</ul>
<h4>Footwear</h4>
<ul>
	<li>Steel - <a href="https://www.oliberte.com/" target="_blank">Oliberte</a> shoes</li>
	<li>Dave - Socks</li>
</ul>
<h3>Unchained Melodies: Favorite Musicians Edition</h3>
https://open.spotify.com/user/steelwagstaff/playlist/0tPfaipAlqSn2NsldtarAz
<h3>Book Wisdom</h3>
Steel shared his favorite poem: George Oppen's "<a href="http://homepages.wmich.edu/~cooneys/poems/oppen.poem.html" target="_blank">Psalm</a>"
<h3></h3>]]></content:encoded>
