		<title><![CDATA[Episode 54: Everything You (N)ever Wanted to Know About Babies]]></title>
		<link>https://otc.steelwagstaff.info/494-2/</link>
		<pubDate>Fri, 29 Apr 2016 12:00:13 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[steel]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://otc.awesomecity.org/?p=494</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[This week Dave and Steel bring back their old friend Amy (Scott) Anderson. Together the trio discuss epic meltdowns, some amazing things that have they've been dying to share with each other during Dave's paternity leave, talk (for a long time) about babies and parenting, share great music they've been digging recently by AURORA, the Strumbellas, Pinegrove, AdriAnne Lenker &amp; Buck Meek, and Whitney, and Amy drops some impressive book wisdom from Paul Kalanithi's touching memoir <em>When Breath Becomes Air</em>.
<h2>Links</h2>
<h3>OTC Quick Hits</h3>
<ul>
 	<li><a href="http://simonegiertz.com/"><span style="font-weight: 400">Simone Giertz</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> has built the queen of </span><a href="https://www.facebook.com/thisisinsiderdesign/videos/235171160157854/?pnref=story"><span style="font-weight: 400">shitty robots</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> [Steel]</span></li>
 	<li><a href="http://www.engadget.com/2016/01/13/michigan-web-firing-drone/"><span style="font-weight: 400">Drones snatching other drones out of the air</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> [Amy]</span></li>
 	<li>Smoked meats &amp; epic fantasy novels are great [Dave]</li>
</ul>
<h3>Assigned Reading</h3>
<ul>
 	<li>Amy for Dave: <em><a href="http://www.amazon.com/Station-Eleven-Emily-John-Mandel/dp/0804172447">Station Eleven</a> </em>by Emily St. John Mandel</li>
 	<li>Amy for Steel: <a href="http://www.amazon.com/When-Breath-Becomes-Paul-Kalanithi/dp/081298840X/ref=sr_1_1?s=books&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1461862260&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=when+breath+becomes+air+by+paul+kalanithi"><em>When Breath Becomes Air</em></a> by Paul Kalanithi</li>
 	<li>Dave for Amy: <a href="http://www.amazon.com/Sebastian-Balloon-Philip-C-Stead/dp/1596439300/ref=sr_1_1?s=books&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1461862291&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=sebastian+and+the+balloon+by+philip+stead"><em>Sebastian and the Balloon</em></a> by Phillip Stead, <a href="http://www.amazon.com/James-Excellence-Childrens-Literature-Awards/dp/0763662291/ref=sr_1_1?s=books&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1461862307&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=sam+and+dave+dig+a+hole"><em>Sam and Dave Dig a Hole</em></a> by Mac Barnett, and <a href="http://www.amazon.com/Harry-Lady-Next-Door-Level/dp/0064440087/ref=sr_1_1?s=books&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1461862324&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=harry+and+the+lady+next+door"><em>Harry and the Lady Next Door</em></a> by Gene Zion</li>
 	<li>Steel for Amy: <a href="http://www.amazon.com/H-Hawk-Helen-Macdonald/dp/0802124739/ref=sr_1_1?s=books&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1461862277&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=h+is+for+hawk"><em>H is for Hawk </em></a>by Helen MacDonald</li>
</ul>
<h3>Unchained Melodies: Songs We're Into Right Now Edition</h3>
https://open.spotify.com/user/steelwagstaff/playlist/49cVp4rlBjXXG7ZBNopgTL
<h3>Book Wisdom</h3>
Amy read a moving passage from Paul Kalanithi's memoir <em>When Breath Becomes Air</em>, in which a dying father gives his final message to his infant daughter.

<small>Featured image: Things not going so well for golfer Jordan Spieth, whose Masters collapse inspired our epic meltdown opening segment on this episode.</small>]]></content:encoded>
