		<title><![CDATA[Episode 61: That One Time at Band Camp ...]]></title>
		<link>https://otc.steelwagstaff.info/episode-61-one-time-band-camp/</link>
		<pubDate>Wed, 10 Aug 2016 19:42:50 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[steel]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://otc.awesomecity.org/?p=527</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[This week Dave and Steel are joined by Steel's old friend Liz Feezor. Together the trio discusses the recent political conventions leading up the US presidential elections, ask Liz all about her career in HR, recent misadventures in Colombia, her past life as a member of the University of Oregon marching band, and her ongoing expertise as a <a href="http://stylishdisaster.com/" target="_blank">style/fashion blogger</a>. We also play great drum music by Wilco, James Brown &amp; Clyde Stubblefield, Beyonce, Radiohead, Fela Kuti, and Van Halen, and Liz shares some book wisdom about the art of writing from Stephen King.
<h2>Links</h2>
<ul>
 	<li>Liz blogs at <a href="http://stylishdisaster.com/" target="_blank">The Stylish Disaster</a>. You can also follow her on <a href="https://www.instagram.com/stylishdisaster/" target="_blank">Instagram</a>.</li>
</ul>
<h3>On Cargo Shorts &amp; the RNC</h3>
https://twitter.com/drewmagary/status/755506490392403968
<h3>On Cargo Shorts Generally</h3>
<ul>
 	<li>From the <a href="http://www.wsj.com/articles/nice-cargo-shorts-youre-sleeping-on-the-sofa-1470082856" target="_blank">WSJ</a> and the story's <a href="http://www.wsj.com/articles/what-happened-after-i-wrote-that-cargo-shorts-story-1470402723" target="_blank">aftermath</a>.</li>
</ul>
<h3>On Khizr Khan</h3>
<ul>
 	<li>His <a href="http://www.cnn.com/videos/politics/2016/07/29/dnc-convention-khizr-khan-father-of-us-muslim-soldier-entire-speech-sot.cnn" target="_blank">moving speech at the DNC</a>.</li>
 	<li><a href="http://www.nytimes.com/2016/08/06/us/khan-soldier-convention-iraq.html" target="_blank">The NYT feature</a> on the Khan family's life pre- and post-DNC.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Unchained Melodies: Drum Line Edition</h3>
https://open.spotify.com/user/steelwagstaff/playlist/0M4xq0XokNZgJuN8OVMh9e

Also, this:

https://youtu.be/LrCHz1gwzTo

and this:

https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PyX-Mjaq8Hk
<h3>Book Wisdom</h3>
Liz shared a brief passage from Stephen King's classic writing memoir <em><a href="https://www.amazon.com/Writing-10th-Anniversary-Memoir-Craft/dp/1439156816" target="_blank">On Writing</a>.</em>

<small>Featured image: Liz playing caixa (a Brazilian snare drum) at <a href="http://fremontartscouncil.org/troll-o-ween/" target="_blank">Trolloween</a> in Seattle in 2011.</small>

]]></content:encoded>
