		<title><![CDATA[Episode 64: The Party! Party! Party! party]]></title>
		<link>https://otc.steelwagstaff.info/episode-64-party-party-party-party/</link>
		<pubDate>Fri, 30 Sep 2016 12:00:58 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[steel]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://otc.awesomecity.org/?p=550</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p class="p1">This week Dave and Steel are joined by Spencer to discuss the latest in Vin Diesel news, their favorite fringe presidential candidates, historical also-rans, and fringe political parties, revive Lost the Plot, share outsider classics from Daniel Johnston, Dan Reeder, The Toadies, They Might Be Giants, Congress-Woman Malinda Jackson Parker, and Leonard Cohen, and hear the calming anti-road book wisdom of the Honku.</p>

<h2 class="p1">Links</h2>
<h3>Perpetual Candidates and Favorite Third Parties</h3>
<ul>
<ul>
 	<li style="font-weight: 400"><span style="font-weight: 400"><a href="http://andy2016.com/" target="_blank">Andrew Basiago</a>, the man we're all backing in 2016.</span></li>
 	<li style="font-weight: 400"><span style="font-weight: 400">Steel thinks more people should know the story of <a href="http://www.miaminewtimes.com/news/meet-the-candidate-6364617" target="_blank">Clennon King</a>, an American legend.</span></li>
 	<li style="font-weight: 400"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Non-human_electoral_candidates" target="_blank">Non human candidates</a> are great too! <span style="font-weight: 400"> Steel's favorite: former Hartlepool mayor </span><span style="font-weight: 400"><a href="http://www.bbc.com/news/uk-england-tees-22375328">H’angus the Monkey</a>.</span></li>
 	<li style="font-weight: 400">Spencer's a big fan of <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cecil_G._Murgatroyd" target="_blank">Cecil G. Murgatroyd</a>. You probably will be too, once you read a little more about his terrific work with the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McGillicuddy_Serious_Party" target="_blank">McGillicuddy Serious Party</a>.</li>
</ul>
</ul>
<h3>Unchained Melodies: Outsider Music</h3>
https://open.spotify.com/user/steelwagstaff/playlist/1IucxbvU7kiCJ4VSsdm6wm
<h3>Book Wisdom</h3>
This week Spencer enlightened us with "<a href="http://www.honku.org/" target="_blank">Honkus</a>," anti road-rage haiku poems by Aaron Naparstek.]]></content:encoded>
