		<title><![CDATA[Episode 68: 2016 in Review, part 1]]></title>
		<link>https://otc.steelwagstaff.info/episode-68-2016-in-review-part-1/</link>
		<pubDate>Wed, 21 Dec 2016 22:02:29 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[steel]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://otc.awesomecity.org/?p=580</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[This year we're trying something new (and awesome). We asked six of our friends to join us for a recap of the year that was, with each of them covering a subject that they're an expert in. We'll be bringing you our 2016 in review in two episodes (this week and next), but this week we were lucky to be joined by Rosie (the social issues that defined 2016: populism, political rhetoric, violence, and environmentalism); Jordan (the year in music, featuring songs from Mick Jenkins + BadBadNotGood, Camp Cope, Mitski, Big Thief, Pinegrove, and Snarky Puppy); and Rose (the year in books &amp; reading).
<h2>Links</h2>
<h3>Social Issues</h3>
<h4>Political Rhetoric</h4>
Michelle Obama's speech at the 2016 DNC

https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4ZNWYqDU948

Theresa May setting out a vision of Conservative leadership as socially responsible and humane (gasp!)

https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ac6VJVDOOz4
<h4>Violence</h4>
Subscribe to journalist <a href="http://thepoliticalnotebook.com/" target="_blank">Torie Rose DeGhett</a>'s "This Week in War" <a href="http://thepoliticalnotebook.us5.list-manage.com/subscribe?u=1c7d675b2370674a1268b23f5&amp;id=e31a814872#_=_" target="_blank">newsletter</a> for weekly updates about violent conflict around the world.
<h3>Unchained Melodies: Favorite Songs and Albums of 2016</h3>
https://open.spotify.com/user/steelwagstaff/playlist/6EKiDeJDzaTNhEQTE2HHMa
<h3>Book Recommendations</h3>
<ul>
 	<li>Rebecca Solnit's <em><a href="http://rebeccasolnit.net/book/men-explain-things-to-me/" target="_blank">Men Explain Things to Me</a> </em>and <em><a href="http://rebeccasolnit.net/book/hope-in-the-dark-untold-histories-wild-possibilities/" target="_blank">Hope in the Dark</a> </em>and <a href="http://rebeccasolnit.net/book/a-paradise-built-in-hell/" target="_blank"><em>A Paradise Built in Hell</em></a>. Anything Solnit writes, really. [Steel]</li>
 	<li>R.J. Palacio's <a href="https://www.amazon.com/Wonder-R-J-Palacio/dp/1480586358" target="_blank"><em>Wonder</em></a> and <a href="http://brandonsanderson.com/" target="_blank">Brandon Sanderson</a>'s fantasy novels! [Dave]</li>
 	<li><a href="http://www.maggiestiefvater.com/" target="_blank">Maggie Steifvater</a>, especially <em>The Scorpio Races </em>or <em>The Raven Cycle</em> [Rose]</li>
</ul>
<h4>Our Top Children's Books of the Year</h4>
<ul>
 	<li><em><a href="http://www.jonagee.com/html/p_books.php" target="_blank">It's Only Stanley</a></em>, Jon Agee and <a href="https://www.amazon.com/Those-Darn-Squirrels-Adam-Rubin/dp/0547576811" target="_blank"><em>Those Darn Squirrels!</em></a>, Adam Rubin &amp; Daniel Salmieri [Dave]</li>
 	<li><a href="http://www.storybreathing.com/order-books/" target="_blank"><em>Journey</em>, <em>Quest</em>, and <em>Return</em></a>, Aaron Becker [Steel]</li>
 	<li><a href="https://www.amazon.com/President-Goes-School-Rick-Walton/dp/1561458929" target="_blank"><em>Mr. President Goes to School</em></a>,<em> </em><a href="http://www.sltrib.com/home/3112080-155/utah-childrens-authors-credit-publishing-boom" target="_blank">Rick Walton</a> [Rose]</li>
</ul>
<h4>Steel's Poetry Tips</h4>
<ul>
 	<li><a href="https://www.amazon.com/Poems-Basil-Bunting/dp/057123500X" target="_blank"><em>The Poems of Basil Bunting</em></a>, ed. Don Share</li>
 	<li><a href="https://www.amazon.com/Sand-Opera-Philip-Metres/dp/1938584090/ref=sr_1_fkmr0_1?s=books&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1482357473&amp;sr=1-1-fkmr0&amp;keywords=sand+opera+phil+metres" target="_blank"><em>Sand Opera</em></a>, Phil Metres</li>
 	<li><a href="https://www.amazon.com/Poems-1962-1997-Robert-Lax/dp/193351776X/ref=sr_1_1?s=books&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1482357487&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=robert+lax" target="_blank"><em>Poems, 1962-1997</em></a>, Robert Lax</li>
</ul>
Finally, Rose has been writing a young adult fantasy book, <em><a href="https://rosecardfaux.com/books/lesser-demons-book-one-in-the-way-reader-series/" target="_blank">Lesser Demons</a></em>. Check it out on her site and share your feedback!

<small>Featured image: Basil Bunting, from the cover of <em>The Poems of Basil Bunting</em>.</small>]]></content:encoded>
